IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg3-civil`
IMPORT `bgg3-criminal`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-scope`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-limits`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-courts`
IMPORT `bgg3-seat`

-- tests-independent: written by an independent test author from the German text alone.
-- Expected values come from ANSWERS.md (written before any .l4 file was opened); none was copied from the encoding.
-- Number = the scenario number in ANSWERS.md; "S" = a seat scenario; a letter suffix = a second assertion for the same scenario.
-- POLARITY: ANSWERS.md asks Art. 83 and Art. 85(1) as "is the appeal BARRED?".  The encoding's layer-1 functions ask "is the appeal ADMISSIBLE?".
--   Translation used below: barred YES = admissible JUST FALSE; bar does not apply = admissible NOTHING (a bar that does not apply is not a grant),
--   except Art. 83(m)'s derogation, which grants ("in Abweichung davon ist die Beschwerde zulaessig"): JUST TRUE.
--   The seat question for Art. 83 asks "is my decision EXCLUDED?" (JUST TRUE = excluded).
-- Convention notes use the short names P1..P6 defined at the top of ANSWERS.md.

-- All facts false: a neutral record for the composite Art 83 question.
DECIDE `no Art 83 facts` IS `Art 83 facts` WITH
    `international law gives a claim to judicial review` IS FALSE
    `federal law or international law gives a claim to the permit` IS FALSE
    `an extradition request is pending from the state of refuge` IS FALSE
    `the Federal Administrative Court decided` IS FALSE
    `a cantonal lower instance decided` IS FALSE
    `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS FALSE
    `the procuring body is one that item (f)(1) reserves` IS FALSE
    `the estimated value of the contract to be awarded` IS 0
    `the threshold under the Public Procurement Act` IS 0
    `the matter is not pecuniary` IS FALSE
    `the matter concerns equality of the sexes` IS FALSE
    `the assistance is in tax matters` IS FALSE
    `the remission concerns the direct federal tax or a cantonal or communal income or profit tax` IS FALSE
    `the case is particularly important for other reasons` IS FALSE
    `the decision was taken in a severe shortage` IS FALSE
    `a claim to the subsidy exists` IS FALSE
    `the customs assessment rests on tariff classification or on the weight of the goods` IS FALSE
    `the concession was the subject of a public tender` IS FALSE

-- ===== Art. 72 =====
#ASSERT `Art 72(1) the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 1 Art 72(1) civil matter
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(a) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the decision in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 2 Art 72(2)(a)
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(1) the public-law decision on recognition, enforcement or legal assistance is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `recognition and enforcement of judgments, or legal assistance in civil matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 3 Art 72(2)(b)(1)
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(2) the public-law decision on keeping a register is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `keeping of a land, civil status, commercial or intellectual-property register` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 4 Art 72(2)(b)(2) land register
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(3) the public-law decision on a name change is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `permission to change a name` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 5 Art 72(2)(b)(3)
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(4) the public-law decision on supervising a foundation is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `supervision of foundations` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 6 Art 72(2)(b)(4) family foundation
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(4) the public-law decision on supervising a foundation is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `supervision of foundations` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- 7 Art 72(2)(b)(4) pension fund excepted. P5: "mit Ausnahme" once met; other reading NOTHING  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST FALSE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): "except" once met is one of the six case-by-case questions (Guide, last ruling of 2026-11-05); the encoder answered NOTHING and the reader JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(5) the public-law decision on supervising an executor or succession-law representative is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `supervision of executors and other succession-law representatives` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 8 Art 72(2)(b)(5)
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b)(6) the public-law decision on child and adult protection is one in immediate connection with civil law` TRUE `child and adult protection` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 9 Art 72(2)(b)(6)
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the public-law decision` TRUE TRUE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 10 Art 72(2)(b) "insbesondere": unlisted but directly connected with civil law
#ASSERT `Art 72(2)(b) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the public-law decision` TRUE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- 11 Art 72(2)(b) public-law, no direct connection, unlisted (tax assessment). Guide: open list / scope, P2 P3
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 1b composite Art 72, civil matter only
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 2b composite Art 72, debt enforcement only

-- ===== Art. 73 =====
