-- ===== Seat layer: a person affected by a decision (a party to civil, criminal or public-law proceedings), in their own facts =====
-- S1: "I am a tenant. The cantonal court found against me on a rent claim of CHF 14 000. I took part. Can I take it to the Federal Supreme Court?"
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE FALSE TRUE 14000 EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S1a tenant, CHF 14000: below the tenancy limit of 15000. P1
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE TRUE 14000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S1b same tenant, no ground for an exception
-- S2: "Same, but the claim was CHF 15 000."
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE FALSE TRUE 15000 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S2 tenant, CHF 15000: enough
-- S3: "Same CHF 14 000 rent claim, but my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance."
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE TRUE 14000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S3 Art 74(2)(a)
-- S4: "A supplier sued me for CHF 25 000 for goods; I lost in the cantonal court of appeal."
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE FALSE FALSE 25000 EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S4 other case, 25000 < 30000
-- S5: "I was a party to an arbitration between two Swiss companies over CHF 8 000; the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 ZPO are met."
#ASSERT `Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S5 national arbitral award, value irrelevant
-- S5b: "I want to write my appeal against the international award in English."
#ASSERT `Art 77(2bis) I may draft my written submission in English` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S5b Art 77(2bis)
-- S5c: "May the Court decide the merits itself in my appeal against an arbitral award (Art 107(2))?"
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` TRUE 107 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S5c Art 107(2) merits decision not applicable
-- S6: "I did not attend the hearing although I was invited; now I want to appeal an CHF 80 000 loss."
#ASSERT `Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S6 Art 76(1)(a)
-- S7: "The court never told me about the proceeding; I am directly hit by the order."
#ASSERT `Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S7 no chance to take part
-- S8: "I am the accused; I took part; I was convicted by the cantonal appeal court."
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `accused person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S8a standing
#ASSERT `Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S8b the decision comes from the last cantonal instance
#ASSERT `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S8c a decision in a criminal matter
-- S9: "I am the victim and private claimant; the court acquitted the accused and rejected my civil claim; I took part."
