-- ===== More seat questions, each with asymmetric facts so a swapped input would show =====
-- "My last cantonal instance decided my civil case."
#ASSERT `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S50a seat Art 75(1) last cantonal instance
#ASSERT `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `another body` EQUALS NOTHING -- S50b seat Art 75(1) a body Art 75(1) does not name. P3
-- "I filed an action of CHF 100 000 straight at the upper court and all parties agreed."
#ASSERT `Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100000 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S51a seat Art 75(2)(c)
#ASSERT `Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S51b seat Art 75(2) upper court as appeal instance
-- "I complained in my appeal against the arbitral award but gave no reasons." / "I gave reasons but did not raise it."
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S52a seat Art 77(3)
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S52b seat Art 77(3) raised, no reasons
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S52c seat Art 77(3) reasons given but the complaint was not raised
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- S52d seat Art 77(3) my appeal is not against an arbitral award: scope P2
-- "Under the Code of Criminal Procedure the upper court decided my case as the sole cantonal instance."
